# V0.25 minimal pilot C3 report — 2026-09-09 (PILOT_NOT_CLAIM)

**PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. Every artefact and every numerical value in this report is PILOT_NOT_CLAIM.**

This is quarantined engineering evidence only. No scientific conclusion, configuration selection, or claim is made.

**Scope of this run.** Evaluation worlds ['V025_PROBE/world/3']; 5 anchor steps x nearest-eligible carrier only; learner seeds ['V025_LEARNER/seed/1', 'V025_LEARNER/seed/2'] (2); learned arms ['FULL', 'DROP_C3'] plus BASELINE, S0, S_UNI; checkpoint epoch 200 (NOT the sealed 2000); training rows restricted to `rows/world-1` (first 5 anchor shards).

## Rows

PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. **These rows were generated by an earlier full-scale run and are reused verbatim.** This minimal pilot consumed only `rows/world-1`, anchor shards 000-004 (5 of 90). The table below is the full inherited row inventory, not the subset actually loaded.

| World | Anchors | Q1/Q2 rows | C3 rows | Bytes |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| V025_PROBE/world/1 | 90 | 87997 | 90 | 270481479 |
| V025_PROBE/world/2 | 90 | 88226 | 90 | 271432834 |

The pilot calibration proxy and every row carry explicit lambda, eta, and kappa exact ratios/hex values. The formal calibration was absent from the launch copy; see DEFECTS.

## Training

PILOT_NOT_CLAIM. **Training is also inherited from the earlier full-scale run and was not re-executed here.** The minimal pilot restores the **epoch-200** checkpoint (2 seeds x {FULL, DROP_C3}); the sealed budget is 2000 epochs and was deliberately *not* used.

Learned arm-seed lineages ran with concurrency 16; external BASELINE seed records were emitted separately. Neutral batches were hoisted once per worker. Each learned lineage completed 2000 source epochs with a checkpoint every 100 epochs; **this report evaluates the epoch-200 checkpoint**.

